/**
 * @page DspCore_Architecture Architecture and planned content
 *
 * Dependency direction: Foundation -> DspCore -> MIDILAR. General utilities
 * belong to Foundation, music theory to MCC, and MIDI interpretation to
 * MIDILAR. DspCore processes signals independently.
 *
 * Content (Core/version, LUT storage, interpolation, generators, single-rate
 * filters, analysis measurements and processing interfaces are implemented;
 * dynamics, broader filter families, response analysis and transforms are
 * planned):
 * - Numeric: scalar precision, ranges and explicit conversion policy.
 * - LUT: 1D, 2D and 3D storage, independent of generators.
 * - Interpolation: linear, bilinear and trilinear.
 * - Generators: periodic tables, noise, envelopes, shaping and windows.
 * - Filters: single-rate FIR/IIR processing and Biquad coefficient design;
 *   SOS, multirate and MIMO filter families are planned.
 * - Dynamics: compressor, limiter and gate boundaries are planned.
 * - Analysis: peak, RMS and envelope followers are implemented; frequency
 *   response, pole-zero and stability analysis are planned.
 * - Processing: typed, non-owning fixed-size sample-block views for algorithms.
 * - Transforms: DFT, IDFT, FFT and IFFT are planned.
 *
 * MIDILAR's musical control layer interprets notes, pedals, RPN/NRPN,
 * controllers and parameter bindings. It may consume DspCore signal processing,
 * but DspCore never interprets MIDI messages.
 *
 * Historical implementations were reviewed at MIDILAR commit
 * bc70ce639f8bb72f79995e1ec742b73aef544112. They are design input, not a
 * compatibility promise. See docs/Design/LegacyDspReview.md in the source
 * checkout for findings and probe evidence.
 *
 * @ref DspCore_Numeric defines the numerical and buffer requirements for
 * migration. Further implementation follows ACTION_PLAN.md phase by phase.
 *
 * DspCore deliberately does not own data streams. A future runtime library
 * will provide audio, MIDI, envelope and event transport, FIFOs, clocks,
 * routing, MIMO graphs and adapters. That layer will pass caller-owned memory
 * to DspCore algorithms through Processing::SampleBlock at its boundary.
 */
